+{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e5d2a3a67e9556c","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→/**\n     2→ * Format a number as a currency string ($X,XXX.XX).\n     3→ */\n     4→export function formatCurrency(amount: number): string {\n     5→  return '$' + amount.toFixed(2).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ',');\n     6→}\n     7→\n     8→/**\n     9→ * Format a rate (0-1) as a percentage string (XX.X%).\n    10→ */\n    11→export function formatPercentage(rate: number): string {\n    12→  return (rate * 100).toFixed(1) + '%';\n    13→}\n    14→\n    15→/**\n    16→ * Calculate tax on an amount.\n    17→ * NOTE: This is a legacy utility function, not currently used in the billing pipeline.\n    18→ */\n    19→export function calculateTax(amount: number, rate: number): number {\n    20→  // BUG: applies rate as whole number instead of decimal\n    21→  // e.g., calculateTax(100, 0.08) returns 800 instead of 8\n    22→  return amount * (rate * 100);\n    23→}\n    24→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83418d6dafb72b2f","session_id":"b05b2ddf-9cd0-4b2e-a4e2-4513919b4a93","uuid":"67cee728-8fd5-4bf4-9fa4-d27bf1348ed4"}
